OpenROAD: a gradient that stops changing ends global placement

bazel-orfs carries this against OpenROAD; it is not upstreamed.

gpl's step length is the coordinate distance divided by the gradient
distance, the Barzilai-Borwein ratio over the backtracking step. When
the gradient distance is exactly zero -- the gradients did not change at
all between the two points -- that ratio is an infinity, and gpl reads
any non-finite step length as a diverged solve and kills the run with

  [ERROR GPL-0305] RePlAce diverged during gradient descent calculation,
  resulting in an invalid step length (Inf or NaN).

But an unchanged gradient is the opposite of a blow-up: it is a solve
with nothing left to move. It shows up on a design the Nesterov loop
cannot drive to the target overflow, where the iterations run to a
standstill rather than to convergence -- a mocked SRAM in bazel-orfs
(sram/sdq_17x64, the mocked variant) reaches it under
global_placement -place_ios, where the movable IO pins follow the cells
they are pulled by and the density penalty has almost no cell area to
work with.

Finish the region instead: a zero gradient distance marks it converged,
with a warning naming the overflow it stopped at, so the placement that
is there is kept and the flow goes on to legalisation. Every other
non-finite step length is still a divergence. A solve whose gradient
still changes never reaches this branch, so nothing changes for a design
that converges.

Retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that ends such a solve itself.

diff --git a/src/gpl/src/nesterovBase.cpp b/src/gpl/src/nesterovBase.cpp
index e274730..b6d5e83 100644
--- a/src/gpl/src/nesterovBase.cpp
+++ b/src/gpl/src/nesterovBase.cpp
@@ -4315,6 +4315,22 @@ bool NesterovBase::nesterovUpdateStepLength()
 
   debugPrint(log_, GPL, "np", 1, "NewStepLength: {:g}", newStepLength);
 
+  // The step length is the coordinate distance over the gradient distance.
+  // A gradient distance of zero means the gradients did not change at all
+  // between the two points: the solve has stopped moving and there is no
+  // Barzilai-Borwein step left to take. That is a placement that is over,
+  // not one that blew up, so finish this region instead of reporting the
+  // infinity it divides out to as a divergence.
+  if (gradDistance_ == 0.0f) {
+    log_->warn(GPL,
+               186,
+               "Gradient unchanged between steps at overflow {:.4f}; "
+               "nothing left to move, finishing global placement.",
+               sum_overflow_unscaled_);
+    isConverged_ = true;
+    return true;
+  }
+
   if (std::isnan(newStepLength) || std::isinf(newStepLength)) {
     isDiverged_ = true;
     return false;
